    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe business-day rule already handled weekends in `BusinessDays.toBusinessDay(...)`. I extended it to also skip the fixed public-holiday list.\n\n**`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/BusinessDays.java`**\n- Added the pinned holiday set: `2026-01-01`, `2026-01-26`, `2026-04-25`, `2026-12-25`, `2026-12-28`.\n- Replaced the single-hop weekend logic with a loop that rolls the date forward one day at a time while it lands on a Saturday, Sunday, or a listed holiday. This correctly chains adjacent skip-days (e.g. a Saturday rolling to a Sunday, or a holiday landing on a weekend/another holiday like the `2026-12-25`/`2026-12-28` cluster).\n\nBoth callers (`BuildOwner`, `RequireDailyLimit`) use `toBusinessDay` and inherit the new behavior automatically. The acceptance test's own `toBusinessDay` helper and `HOLIDAYS` set match the production implementation exactly.",
